WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.032
Raj: Let me tail the log. The failed queries point to one upstream forwarder with no reply.

2
00:00:07.032 --> 00:00:13.392
Hannah: Does A have more than one target? That could explain the intermittent failures.

3
00:00:13.392 --> 00:00:20.544
Raj: Two targets. One replies, one doesn't. B's configured targets are different.

4
00:00:20.544 --> 00:00:27.384
Priya: Just to confirm, we know the failing endpoint, right? We don't know why it's there yet.

5
00:00:27.384 --> 00:00:34.248
Lukas: Check the inventory and recent changes. Don't remove an endpoint based only on one timeout.

6
00:00:34.248 --> 00:00:41.304
Anika: Our working hypothesis is a stale forwarding target. The retirement record needs confirmation.

7
00:00:41.304 --> 00:00:48.624
Hannah: I'll check the approved configuration. We also need to know B preserves the private view.

8
00:00:48.624 --> 00:00:54.504
Priya: What's the ETA? Can we prepare B without changing any clients yet?

9
00:00:54.504 --> 00:01:01.824
Lukas: Yes. Check capacity, reachability, and the required private names before proposing a switch.

10
00:01:01.824 --> 00:01:08.640
Raj: I'm on it. About three minutes for the checklist. No public resolver shortcut.

